r. We will simply recapture the knight.} 9.bxc3 9...d5 {This is the engine's top choice, equalizing the position. We next improve the rook by giving a check on e1.} 10.Re1+ 10...Be6 {Black keeps the tension on the queenside and blocks the check by playing ...Be6. This is a mistake, yet it happened in 22% of the games! Here, we should gladly grab the bishop on b4!} 11.cxb4 11...dxc4 {Black thinks they've got out of trouble.} 12.d5 {But now we deliver a fork on d5 and win a piece!} *

[Event "Chapter 1: The c3 and d4 Italian / Study 1: Black Plays 7...Nxe4 (Main Line) / Variation 6"]
[Site "https://chessly.com/courses/6cdd46e2-7bff-4f8b-bfcf-aeddd9745e6c/chapters/74208d2e-70c1-4233-9a81-2a7ebcff6773/studies/ced87143-df87-4aaf-9e5f-b2f25342cb7f/lines"]

